          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em super Poincaré Lie algebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            extension of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Euclidean+group"} super Euclidean group
            (except for the signature of the metric).
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{N}
            and consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} ^{d-1,1}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
            the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S \in Rep(Spin(d-1,1))
          %p
            be a real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"}> Majorana spinor
            ), which has the property (
            %a{:href => "Majorana+spinor#SpinorToVectorBilinearPairing"}> def.
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Majorana+spinor#SpinorToVectorPairing"} prop.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma \;\colon\; S \otimes S \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
          %p which is
          %ol
            %li
              %p symmetric:
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance"} equivariant
                (a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                of
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
          %p
            For a classification of spin representations with this property see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
            the sections
            %em
              %a{:href => "spin+representation#RealIrreducibleSpinRepresentationInLorentzSignature"} real irreducible spin representations in Lorentz signature
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "spin+representation#SuperPoincareBrackets"} super Poincaré brackets
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Majorana+spinor#TheSpinorPairingToVectors"} The spinor pairing to vectors
          #SuperPoincare.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong super Poincaré Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{siso}_S(d-1,1)
              of
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with symmetric and
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \colon S \otimes S \to \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi S
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              underlying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              taken in odd degree)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝔦𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⋉
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi S \longrightarrow \mathfrak{siso}_S(d-1,1)
                    \\longrightarrow \mathfrak{iso}(d-1,1) \simeq \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1} \ltimes \mathfrak{so}(d-1,1)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
              of elements in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(d-1,1)
              with those in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is the given
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
              with those on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is trivial, and the Lie bracket of two elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_1, s_2 \in S
              is given by
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [s_1,s_2] \coloneqq \Gamma(s_1,s_2)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It is precisely the symmetry and
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              that makes this a well defined
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
              on elements in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "-equivariance" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o \in \mathfrak{so}(d-1,1)
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_1, s_2 \in S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi o
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi o
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi o
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma([o,s_1], s_2)
                    +
                    \\Gamma(s_1, [o,s_2])
                    \=
                    [o, \Gamma(s_1,s_2)]
                    \\,.
          #CEAlgebraOfSuperPoincare.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              By the general discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{siso}_S(D-1,1)
              by its CE super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{siso}_S(D-1,1))
              “of
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left-invariant+1-forms"} left-invariant 1-forms
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega_a{}^b\}_{a,b}
              for the canonical basis of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+Lie+algebra"} special orthogonal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+Lie+algebra"} matrix Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(D-1,1)
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi_\alpha\}_\alpha
              for a corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                      %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{siso}_N(d-1,1))
              is generated on
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^a\}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega^{ a b}\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
              %li
                %p
                  and elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi^\alpha\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
            %p with the differential defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \omega^{a b} = \omega^a{}_b \wedge \omega^{b c}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} e^{a } = \omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b + \frac{i}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^a \psi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \psi = \frac{1}{4} \omega^{ a b} \wedge \Gamma_{a b} \psi
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Removing all terms involving
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              here yields the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+algebra"} super translation algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo ;
                          %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{D;N}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The abstract generators in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraOfSuperPoincare"}
              are identified with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+1-forms"} left invariant 1-forms
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-translation+group"} super-translation group
              as follows.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^a, \theta^\alpha)
              be the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d|N}
              underlying the super translation group. Then the identification is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo =
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^\alpha = d \theta^\alpha
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mfrac
                          %mi i
                          %mn 2
                        %mover
                          %mi θ
                          %mo ¯
                        %msup
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi a
                        %mi d
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^a = d x^a + \frac{i}{2} \overline{\theta} \Gamma^a d \theta
                  \.
            %p
              This then gives the formula for the differential of the super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraOfSuperPoincare"}
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi a
                            %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                            %mover
                              %mi θ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mi d
                            %mi θ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mi θ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mi d
                            %mi θ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                            %mover
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    d e^a &amp; = d (d x^a + \frac{i}{2} \overline{\theta} \Gamma^a d \theta)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} d \overline{\theta}\Gamma^a d \theta
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} \overline{\psi}\Gamma^a \psi
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#LieAlgebraCohomology Lie algebra cohomology
          %p
            The super Poincaré Lie algebra has, on top of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cocycles
            that it inherits from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(n)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+algebra"} super translation algebra
          %p
            The following theorem has been stated at various placed in the physics literature (known there as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            for
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            for super-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
