                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 11
            is the one that induces the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
          %p
            All these cocycles are controled by the relevant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fierz+identities"} Fierz identities
          %h3#extensions Extensions
          %h4#super_algebra_extensions
            Super
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super L-infinity algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} infinity-Lie algebra cohomology
            of the super Poincaré Lie algebra corresponding to the
            %a{:href => "#LieAlgebraCohomology"} above
            cocycles involves
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %strong super-Poincaré Lie algebra
          %h4#PolyvectorExtensions Extended super Poincaré Lie algebra – Polyvector extensions
          %p
            The super-Poincaré Lie algebra has a class of super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extensions"} Lie algebra extensions
            called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+supersymmetry"} extended supersymmetry
            algebras or
            %em polyvector extensions
            , because they involve additional generators that transforn as skew-symmetric
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensors"} tensors
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ACDP"} ACDP
          %p
            For instance the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+Lie+algebra"}> M-theory Lie algebra
            ” is a polyvector extension of the super Poincaré Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{siso}_{N=1}(10,1)
            by polyvectors of rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p=5
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            in the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PolyvectorExtensionsAsAutomorphismLieAlgebras"} Polyvector extensions as automorphism Lie algebras
          %h5#as_current_algebras_of_the_gs_super_branes
            As current algebras of the GS super
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            The polyvector extensions arise as the super Lie algebras of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super+p-brane+sigma-models"} Green-Schwarz super p-brane sigma-models
            (
            %a{:href => "#AGIT89"}> AGIT 89
            ).
          %h5#PolyvectorExtensionsAsAutomorphismLieAlgebras
            As automorphism Lie algebras of Lie
            = succeed "-superalgebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            At least some of the
            %a{:href => "#PolyvectorExtensions"} polyvector extensions
            of the super Poincaré Lie algebra arise as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            super Lie algebras of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-algebra"} Lie n-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} extensions
            classified by the cocycles discussed above.
          %p
            For instance the automorphisms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            gives the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+Lie+algebra"}> M-theory Lie algebra
            ”-extension of super-Poincaré in 11-dimensions (
            %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
            ). This is also discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "supergravity+Lie+3-algebra#Polyvector"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra – Polyvector extensions
          %h3#Contractions Contractions
          %p
            One may consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+breaking"} breaking
            super-Poincaré invariance by passage to non-relativistic or ultrarelativistic limits, formally understood as taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/speed+of+light"} speed of light
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
