            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-models"} Green-Schwarz sigma-models
          %h3#PolyvectorExtensionRefs Polyvector extensions
          %p
            The Polyvector extensions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 32
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{10,1|32})
            (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+super+Lie+algebra"}> M-theory super Lie algebra
            ”) were first considered in
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFre82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravity.pdf", :title => "Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup"} Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan-Willem+van+Holten"}> Jan-Willem van Holten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoine+Van+Proeyen"} Antoine Van Proeyen
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                  supersymmetry algebras in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 4
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d=2,3,4 \,mod\, 8
                J.Phys. A15, 3763 (1982).
          %p
            Polyvector extensions were found as the algebra of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super+p-branes"} Green-Schwarz super p-branes
            in
          %ul
            %li#AGIT89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jerome+Gauntlett"} Jerome Gauntlett
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological Extensions of the Supersymmetry Algebra for Extended Objects
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/26393?ln=en"} spire
          %p reviewed in section 8.8. of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              , José M. Izquierdo,
              %em Lie Groups, Lie Algebras, Cohomology and Some Applications in Physics
              , Cambridge monographs of mathematical physics, (1995)
          %p
            and specifically for super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            this discussion is in
          %ul
            %li
              Hanno Hammer,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological Extensions of Noether Charge Algebras carried by D-p-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711009"} arXiv:hep-th/9711009
          %p
            The role of polyvector extended supersymmetry algebras in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            is further highlighted in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"}> Paul Townsend
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-Brane Democracy
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9507048"}> arXiv:hep-th/9507048
              )
          %p A comprehensive account and classification of the polyvector extensions of the super Poincaré Lie algebras is in
          %ul
            %li#ACDP
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmiti+Alekseevsky"}> Dmiti Alekseevsky
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vicente+Cort%C3%A9s"} Vicente Cortés
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoine+Van+Proeyen"} Antoine Van Proeyen
              %em Polyvector Super-Poincaré Algebras
              Commun.Math.Phys. 253 (2004) 385-422 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0311107"}> arXiv:hep-th/0311107
              )
          %h3#ReferencesLieAlgebraCohomology Super Lie algebra cohomology
          %p
            Discussion of the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
            goes back to work on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+models"} Green-Schwarz sigma models
            in
          %ul
            %li#AzcarragaTownsend89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superspace geometry and classification of supersymmetric extended objects
              %strong 62
              (1989) 2579-2582 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.62.2579"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.62.2579
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/284635"} spire:284635
          %p A rigorous classification of these cocycles was later given in
          %ul
            %li#Brandt12-13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedemann+Brandt"}> Friedemann Brandt
                ,
                %em Supersymmetry algebra cohomology
              %p
                %em I: Definition and general structure
                J. Math. Phys.51:122302, 2010, (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2118"}> arXiv:0911.2118
                )
              %p
                %em> II: Primitive elements in 2 and 3 dimensions
                , J. Math. Phys. 51 (2010) 112303 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.2978"}> arXiv:1004.2978
                )
              %p
                %em> III: Primitive elements in four and five dimensions
                , J. Math. Phys. 52:052301, 2011 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.2102"}> arXiv:1005.2102
                )
              %p
                %em>
                  IV: Primitive elements in all dimensions from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=4
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                , J. Math. Phys. 54, 052302 (2013) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.6211"}> arXiv:1303.6211
                )
          %p A classification of some special cases of signature/supersymmetry of this is also in the following (using a computer algebra system):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Movshev"}> Mikhail Movshev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
                %em Homology of Lie algebra of supersymmetries
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4731"}> arXiv:1011.4731
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Movshev"}> Mikhail Movshev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homology of Lie algebra of supersymmetries and of super Poincaré Lie algebra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.0335"} arXiv:1106.0335
          %p
            For applications of this classification see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
          %p
            An introduction to the exceptional fermionic cocycles on the super Poincaré Lie algebra, and their description using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
          %ul#BaezHuerta10
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.0551"}> arXiv:0909.0551
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry II
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3436"}> arXiv:1003.34360
                )
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Division Algebras, Supersymmetry and Higher Gauge Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.3385"} arXiv:1106.3385
          %p
            This subsumes some of the results in (
            %a{:href => "#AzcarragaTownsend89"}> Azcárraga-Townend
            )
          %p
            Discussion of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+extensions"} L-∞ extensions
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FSS13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
          %p
            A direct constructions of ordinary (Lie algebraic) extensions of the super Poincaré Lie algebra by means of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras"} division algebras
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Jerzy Lukierski, Francesco Toppan,
              %em Generalized Space-time Supersymmetries, Division Algebras and Octonionic M-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://cbpfindex.cbpf.br/publication_pdfs/NF00102.2010_08_03_10_47_48.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebra+and+supersymmetry"} division algebra and supersymmetry
          %p On the notion of contraction used for non-Lorentzian limits:
          %ul
            %li#IW53
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erdal+%C4%B0n%C3%B6n%C3%BC"}> Erdal İnönü
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugene+Wigner"} Eugene Wigner
              = succeed "." do
                %em On the Contraction of Groups and Their Representations
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.39.6.510"} doi
          %p Discussion of the Carrollian- and Galilean limits:
          %ul
            %li#KN23
              %p
                Konstantinos Koutrolikos, Mojtaba Najafizadeh.
                %em Super-Carrollian and super-Galilean field theories.
                Physical Review D 108, no. 12 (2023): 125014. (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.108.125014"}> doi
                ).
            %li#BFG23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joaquim+Gomis"} Joaquim Gomis
                %em A non-lorentzian primer.
                SciPost Physics Lecture Notes (2023): 069. (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.21468/SciPostPhysLectNotes.69"}> doi
                ).
